on free iff it embeds into a finite free R-module. Finiteness on M and both implications are retained."}
{"schema":"maththm.phase2-final.worker-source-review.v1","candidate_id":"candidate.stacks.1e4948e80c99f3b422dfc59b","decision":"source_equivalence_approved","reviewer":"chatgpt-final-phase2-worker-4-2026-11-03-continuation","source_first_review":true,"proof_reviewed":false,"prior_stage_a_reviewer":"chatgpt-stage-a","prior_stage_b_reviewer":"chatgpt-stageb-worker-2","source_revision":"a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14","source_file":"more-algebra.tex","source_line":4913,"source_label":"lemma-flat-torsion-free","original_source_statement_tex":"\\label{lemma-flat-torsion-free}\nLet $R$ be a domain. Any flat $R$-module is torsion free.","stage_a_artifact":"harvest/phase2_chat_stage_a/more-algebra/batch_02_sections_16_30/RECONSTRUCTIONS.jsonl","stage_a_blob_sha":"e18557b5b5a6d88bb452019ad42dbad9167ea0bd","stage_b_result_file":"work/stageb-parallel/worker-2/results/more-algebra/section-4774.jsonl","stage_b_result_blob_sha":"fb39a3ed59fa48a4348184dd593531e2c7f33480","phase3_review_file":"work/phase3-parallel/worker-2/proof_reviews/more-algebra/section-4774.jsonl","phase3_review_blob_sha":"63839174c60e10ffa7bdc81f1592aa0d20e91000","phase2_proposal_file":"work/phase3-parallel/worker-2/phase2_proposals/more-algebra/section-4774.jsonl","phase2_proposal_blob_sha":"78dfb1b8cbd9cb940b30628c38b2a9ccf6b4b70b","statement":"Let $R$ be a domain. Any flat $R$-module is torsion free.","hypotheses":["Let $R$ be a domain."],"conclusions":["Any flat $R$-module is torsion free."],"logical_form":"source_assertion","structured_cases":null,"equivalence_sides":null,"approved_content_sha256":"fbb10c9fbd44c1dda4bf003d0d35e22eb5b209116ed598aa35fd2d9498f52413","semantic_review_note":"Every flat module over a domain is torsion free. The domain and flatness assumptions remain, with no converse claimed."}
{"schema":"maththm.phase2-final.worker-source-review.v1","candidate_id":"candidate.stacks.3a6adfd3a674339bfdbf5fc6","decision":"source_equivalence_approved","reviewer":"chatgpt-final-phase2-worker-4-2026-11-03-continuation","source_first_review":true,"proof_reviewed":false,"prior_stage_a_reviewer":"chatgpt-stage-a","prior_stage_b_reviewer":"chatgpt-stageb-worker-2","source_revision":"a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14","source_file":"more-algebra.tex","source_line":4924,"source_label":"lemma-valuation-ring-torsion-free-flat","original_source_statement_tex":"\\label{lemma-valuation-ring-torsion-free-flat}\nLet $A$ be a valuation ring.\nAn $A$-module $M$ is flat over $A$ if and only if $M$ is torsion free.","stage_a_artifact":"harvest/phase2_chat_stage_a/more-algebra/batch_02_sections_16_30/RECONSTRUCTIONS.jsonl","stage_a_blob_sha":"e18557b5b5a6d88bb452019ad42dbad9167ea0bd","stage_b_result_file":"work/stageb-parallel/worker-2/results/more-algebra/section-4774.jsonl","stage_b_result_blob_sha":"fb39a3ed59fa48a4348184dd593531e2c7f33480","phase3_review_file":"work/phase3-parallel/worker-2/proof_reviews/more-algebra/section-4774.jsonl","phase3_review_blob_sha":"63839174c60e10ffa7bdc81f1592aa0d20e91000","phase2_proposal_file":"work/phase3-parallel/worker-2/phase2_proposals/more-algebra/section-4774.jsonl","phase2_proposal_blob_sha":"78dfb1b8cbd9cb940b30628c38b2a9ccf6b4b70b","statement":"Let $A$ be a valuation ring.\nAn $A$-module $M$ is flat over $A$ if and only if $M$ is torsion free.","hypotheses":["Let $A$ be a valuation ring."],"conclusions":["An $A$-module $M$ is flat over $A$ if and only if $M$ is torsion free."],"logical_form":"source_assertion","structured_cases":null,"equivalence_sides":null,"approved_content_sha256":"ae572b3a5d18ec9bb8d005bc24d2103567b3561d5fe1fac9d90f9235333d0e60","semantic_review_note":"Over a valuation ring, an arbitrary module is flat if and only if it is torsion free. The special valuation-ring hypothesis and biconditional distinguish it from the general-domain lemma."}
{"schema":"maththm.phase2-final.worker-source-review.v1","candidate_id":"candidate.stacks.68ba356a69a7704dd7a9a41c","decision":"source_equivalence_approved","reviewer":"chatgpt-final-phase2-worker-4-2026-11-03-continuation","source_first_review":true,"proof_reviewed":false,"prior_stage_a_reviewer":"chatgpt-stage-a","prior_stage_b_reviewer":"chatgpt-stageb-worker-2","source_revision":"a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14","source_file":"more-algebra.tex","source_line":4995,"source_label":"lemma-hom-into-torsion-free","original_source_statement_tex":"\\label{lemma-hom-into-torsion-free}\nLet $R$ be a domain. Let $M$, $N$ be $R$-modules.\nIf $N$ is torsion free, so is $\\Hom_R(M, N)$.","stage_a_artifact":"harvest/phase2_chat_stage_a/more-algebra/batch_02_sections_16_30/RECONSTRUCTIONS.jsonl","stage_a_blob_sha":"e18557b5b5a6d88bb452019ad42dbad9167ea0bd","stage_b_result_file":"work/stageb-parallel/worker-2/results/more-algebra/section-4774.jsonl","stage_b_result_blob_sha":"fb39a3ed59fa48a4348184dd593531e2c7f33480","phase3_review_file":"work/phase3-parallel/worker-2/proof_reviews/more-algebra/section-4774.jsonl","phase3_review_blob_sha":"63839174c60e10ffa7bdc81f1592aa0d20e91000","phase2_proposal_file":"work/phase3-parallel/worker-2/phase2_proposals/more-algebra/section-4774.jsonl","phase2_proposal_blob_sha":"78dfb1b8cbd9cb940b30628c38b2a9ccf6b4b70b","statement":"Let $R$ be a domain. Let $M$, $N$ be $R$-modules.\nIf $N$ is torsion free, so is $\\Hom_R(M, N)$.","hypotheses":["Let $R$ be a domain. Let $M$, $N$ be $R$-modules."],"conclusions":["If $N$ is torsion free, so is $\\Hom_R(M, N)$."],"logical_form":"source_setup_then_assertion","structured_cases":null,"equivalence_sides":null,"approved_content_sha256":"257a8e02dc54eb44fd00fbbe1c0665584dc2b25de9bb138856055e886831df02","semantic_review_note":"For domain R, if N is torsion free then Hom_R(M,N) is torsion free for any R-module M. No finiteness assumption on M is added."}
